00:06:44,660 --> 00:06:50,620
 feels really good here, and then we've got physical buttons for our cruise control, and

99
00:06:50,620 --> 00:06:53,340
 our track volume selection, all that stuff.

100
00:06:53,340 --> 00:06:57,900
 These lower buttons feel really nice in hand, they're kind of grippy and knurled, which

101
00:06:57,900 --> 00:06:58,900
 feels very good.

102
00:06:58,900 --> 00:07:02,020
 And then you've got a bunch of configurations here for your gauge clusters.

103
00:07:02,020 --> 00:07:06,620
 Of course you can customize this, variations on a theme from what we've seen from Lexus

104
00:07:06,620 --> 00:07:10,330
 and Toyota and their other cluster designs.

105
00:07:10,330 --> 00:07:13,090
 So you've got a nice EcoCharge power meter there.

106
00:07:13,090 --> 00:07:16,250
 I like this dual pod layout, it's pretty useful.

107
00:07:16,250 --> 00:07:20,000
 Let's delve into this infotainment system some.

108
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:25,560
 So we've got our native navigation, you've got some different widgets here showing you

109
00:07:25,560 --> 00:07:31,560
 your music, your phone, your drive mode, and then you can customize all of this stuff,

110
00:07:31,560 --> 00:07:32,560
 which is great.

111
00:07:32,560 --> 00:07:37,790
 You can see your weather, your media, and then save all of that.

112
00:07:37,790 --> 00:07:39,430
 Very cool.

113
00:07:39,430 --> 00:07:44,470
 The climate menu doesn't really give you much more functionality, I guess you can customize

114
00:07:44,470 --> 00:07:50,090
 different things like S-Flow, de-icer, and then auto-adjust the seat temperature, but

115
00:07:50,090 --> 00:07:54,370
 most of your controls for temperature and fan speed are easily accessible right here.

116
00:07:54,370 --> 00:07:58,090
 Some of these icons are a little bit small, but you've got a little ridge underneath the

117
00:07:58,090 --> 00:08:01,410
 screen to rest and stabilize your hand, which I appreciate.

118
00:08:01,410 --> 00:08:06,710
 Of course, heated and ventilated seats, heated steering wheel, all that stuff, and then your

119
00:08:06,710 --> 00:08:08,830
 temperature control is right there.

120
00:08:08,830 --> 00:08:13,990
 Volume is a nice slider, and like I mentioned earlier, we only get a reverse camera in this

121
00:08:13,990 --> 00:08:19,280
 premium Lexus ES 350h.

122
00:08:19,280 --> 00:08:21,200
 Anything else I need to cover?

123
00:08:21,200 --> 00:08:28,360
 Here are the visors, they slide, we've got a big panoramic sunroof there, the seats are

124
00:08:28,360 --> 00:08:32,800
 nice and thin, but very well padded and comfortable, appreciate that.

125
00:08:32,800 --> 00:08:37,680
 You can hide your water bottle and cup holders with this, and there's a little bit of storage

126
00:08:37,680 --> 00:08:41,360
 underneath here, as well as some ambient lighting that you probably can't see too well during

127
00:08:41,360 --> 00:08:43,590
 the day right now.

128
00:08:43,590 --> 00:08:52,170
 Let's head out onto the road, we will enable our route, we've got a route to scan here,

129
00:08:52,170 --> 00:09:08,100
 and let's give you guys some first driving impressions on this new Lexus ES.

130
00:09:08,100 --> 00:09:21,210
 Doing Austin Powers four-point turn here, looks like we're going right, so we don't

131
00:09:21,210 --> 00:09:23,850
 need to wait ten minutes for this traffic light to turn.

132
00:09:23,850 --> 00:09:31,760
 The biggest thing you notice with this new ES is just how smooth and torquey it is.

133
00:09:31,760 --> 00:09:34,910
 Very little engine noise, very little NVH.

134
00:09:34,910 --> 00:09:41,340
 The ride is slightly firmer than I was expecting it to be, for what this car is, but once you

135
00:09:41,340 --> 00:09:46,660
 get up to speed, it seems really nicely damped, and really well isolated.

136
00:09:46,660 --> 00:10:01,270
 Good body control, it's a nice blend between sporting intentions but also good ride comfort.

137
00:10:01,270 --> 00:10:12,500
 Throttle response, even in normal mode, is pretty instant, and overall power feels great.

138
00:10:12,500 --> 00:10:19,310
 Brake pedal calibration, linear, responsive, none of that hybrid squish that sometimes

139
00:10:19,310 --> 00:10:22,760
 we get in Toyota and Lexus hybrids.

140
00:10:22,760 --> 00:10:26,720
 Everything just feels a little bit tighter, a little bit better calibrated in this new

141
00:10:26,720 --> 00:10:29,190
 ES.

142
00:10:29,190 --> 00:10:35,580
 And I feel like even though this is a pretty basic, simple interior, it's functional enough,

143
00:10:35,580 --> 00:10:39,740
 the stuff that is in the screen is easily and quickly accessible, and the materials

144
00:10:39,740 --> 00:10:45,380
 feel like an improvement over what Lexus has maybe been giving us over the last couple

145
00:10:45,380 --> 00:10:51,520
 years in some of their new products.

146
00:10:51,520 --> 00:11:17,780
 No shakes, no rattles, very little wind noise in this new ES, 44 horsepower for getting

147
00:11:17,780 --> 00:11:18,780
 in front of the Prius.

148
00:11:18,780 --> 00:11:31,420
 Alright.

149
00:11:31,420 --> 00:11:40,970
 It also feels surprisingly light and nimble on its feet, agile, I have good visibility.

150
00:11:40,970 --> 00:11:44,450
 If you want the full summary, it's a perfectly fine automobile.

151
00:11:44,450 --> 00:11:50,050
 I don't think it's outrageously priced, I could do with some premium plus features in

152
00:11:50,050 --> 00:11:51,590
 this.

153
00:11:51,590 --> 00:11:57,650
 Now the EV has a luxury trim, but you save a little bit of money with the EV too, trim

154
00:11:57,650 --> 00:11:58,650
 to trim.

155
00:11:58,650 --> 00:12:00,610
 This is about $2,000 going with the EV.

156
00:12:00,610 --> 00:12:05,090
 Of course you could always get this in all-wheel drive if you need it, but this has great traction

157
00:12:05,090 --> 00:12:09,630
 in the drive as a front-wheel drive platform.

158
00:12:09,630 --> 00:12:13,750
 First time Lexus is ever offering the ES as an all-wheel drive configuration.

159
00:12:13,750 --> 00:12:18,490
 I mean, they have the powertrains, why not swap them in?

160
00:12:18,490 --> 00:12:23,910
 It's kind of a surprise seeing Toyota add so many EV options to the lineup, it's basically

161
00:12:23,910 --> 00:12:29,280
 just the same packs that we've seen with the BZs, and they're just putting them in a bunch

