00:12:29,280 --> 00:12:33,610
 of different models.

163
00:12:33,610 --> 00:12:40,490
 But the luxury ES has a lot more features, it's got lounge chairs in the back.

164
00:12:40,490 --> 00:12:45,970
 But if you just want a Lexus ES, the bare necessity, the bare-bones experience that

165
00:12:45,970 --> 00:12:52,090
 gives you the luxurious feel and the look, this ES 350h I think is probably going to

166
00:12:52,090 --> 00:12:53,090
 be the way to go.

167
00:12:53,090 --> 00:12:59,010
 It's got tons and tons of driving range as a hybrid, super fuel-efficient, very comfortable.

168
00:12:59,010 --> 00:13:04,640
 I think it kind of hits the nail on the head and does what you need it to do.

169
00:13:04,640 --> 00:13:09,160
 Really, the only thing I feel like I'm lacking in here is the Mark Levinson sound and a 360

170
00:13:09,160 --> 00:13:15,810
 cam, and you can option those things.

171
00:13:15,810 --> 00:13:33,480
 Let's do a sound system test with our standard sound system here, and see what that's like.

172
00:13:33,480 --> 00:13:47,410
 Volume controls here to the left, we're going to get a left lane on some of this traffic.

173
00:13:47,410 --> 00:13:49,530
 Still very clear.

174
00:13:49,530 --> 00:14:19,510
 Honestly, first impressions, this premium/base model sound system sounds great.

175
00:14:19,510 --> 00:14:23,030
 I mean, they're still calling the base model a premium, and then you can upgrade to the

176
00:14:23,030 --> 00:14:33,380
 premium plus with the hybrid, and you get the EV if you want to get into luxury, etc.

177
00:14:33,380 --> 00:14:36,980
 Maybe not as sweet as the Mark Levinson would be.

178
00:14:36,980 --> 00:14:39,780
 I haven't listened to the Mark Levinson yet, but this is great.

179
00:14:39,780 --> 00:14:51,100
 For $53,000, this is a fantastic sound system.

180
00:14:51,100 --> 00:14:59,710
 I also feel like this is a really nice interior direction for a Lexus.

181
00:14:59,710 --> 00:15:03,850
 I like the functionality, I like the layout and organization of everything.

182
00:15:03,850 --> 00:15:05,910
 It's just easy to acclimate to and easy to use.

183
00:15:05,910 --> 00:15:10,990
 I jumped into this car and immediately had an idea of where everything should be, and

184
00:15:10,990 --> 00:15:15,200
 even in the infotainment where stuff could be buried a little bit deeper here and there,

185
00:15:15,200 --> 00:15:19,990
 I felt like I had a good grasp on where different settings should be.

186
00:15:19,990 --> 00:15:24,710
 They pretty much moved a lot of the settings into here, instead of splitting them up between

187
00:15:24,710 --> 00:15:28,940
 the screen and the gauge cluster, which I appreciate.

188
00:15:28,940 --> 00:15:31,370
 I don't really have any complaints about this interior space.

189
00:15:31,370 --> 00:15:35,090
 I think it does exactly what it needs to do for the Lexus ES.

190
00:15:35,090 --> 00:15:41,850
 It's the exterior design that might be a point of contention for some buyers, whether they're

191
00:15:41,850 --> 00:15:48,050
 kind of into the swooping lines and crazy hard surfaces and all the things that Lexus

192
00:15:48,050 --> 00:15:50,330
 has done with their new design language.

193
00:15:50,330 --> 00:15:52,970
 I think people will ultimately get used to it.

194
00:15:52,970 --> 00:15:54,620
 We always do.

195
00:15:54,620 --> 00:15:58,980
 It's a pretty striking car to look at on first impressions, and it might turn off a few buyers

196
00:15:58,980 --> 00:16:16,030
 who want something a bit more sedate and subdued, which is understandable.

197
00:16:16,030 --> 00:16:19,790
 On a pretty bumpy section of road here, NVH is good.

198
00:16:19,790 --> 00:16:26,920
 Again, it's just a couple bumps are a bit more harsh than I was expecting with this

199
00:16:26,920 --> 00:16:27,920
 ES.

200
00:16:27,920 --> 00:16:38,790
 It's not as Lexus soft as I wanted it to be.

201
00:16:38,790 --> 00:16:40,990
 Driving around the city, it's super comfy.

202
00:16:40,990 --> 00:16:47,130
 You've got throttle control is nice and linear, no complaints there.

203
00:16:47,130 --> 00:16:52,650
 It'll remain in EV mode pretty readily at lower speeds, that transition from EV to internal

204
00:16:52,650 --> 00:16:59,990
 combustion engine turning on is seamless, it's silent, barely notice it.

205
00:16:59,990 --> 00:17:34,790
 I love how responsive this powertrain is.

206
00:17:34,790 --> 00:17:50,740
 There's no adaptive suspension in this 350H Premium, so changing drive modes doesn't really

207
00:17:50,740 --> 00:17:58,570
 do a whole lot except for steering, weight, and throttle response.

208
00:17:58,570 --> 00:18:03,370
 Even though it's a much longer and larger car, it doesn't feel difficult or tedious to

209
00:18:03,370 --> 00:18:04,370
 place on the road.

210
00:18:04,370 --> 00:18:15,280
 It's still narrow enough to fit through small gaps.

211
00:18:15,280 --> 00:18:19,320
 Seats are super comfortable, and great visibility from this driving position too.

212
00:18:19,320 --> 00:18:24,660
 I don't know if we're going to get a chance to go on the highway with this route, so I

213
00:18:24,660 --> 00:18:27,900
 will just kind of sum up some thoughts on that.

214
00:18:27,900 --> 00:18:35,780
 The Toyota Safety, or sorry, Lexus Safety Assist 4.0, or whatever it's called, is fine.

215
00:18:35,780 --> 00:18:38,950
 It's about the same as it's always been.

216
00:18:38,950 --> 00:18:42,750
 The lane centering works well enough, it's not perfect.

217
00:18:42,750 --> 00:18:46,510
 The lane change is something I could probably just do without.

218
00:18:46,510 --> 00:18:48,390
 You have to keep your hands on the wheel, it does okay.

219
00:18:48,390 --> 00:18:51,950
 There's a lot of beeping going on, it's whatever.

220
00:18:51,950 --> 00:18:56,150
 Adaptive cruise control, following distance changes are easily made right here, and it's

221
00:18:56,150 --> 00:19:00,430
 pretty much the same button layout that we've had in a lot of other Toyota models and Lexus

222
00:19:00,430 --> 00:19:04,710
 models but just with this new pad here.

223
00:19:04,710 --> 00:19:08,110
 And it seems to work just fine, everything is nicely differentiated, and I like that

224
00:19:08,110 --> 00:19:13,620
